  "worked_solution": "Let $P$ be the matrix that represents the rotation, $Q$ be the matrix that represents the stretching, and $R$ be the matrix that represents the shearing. These are given by the following elementary transformation matrices:\n\n$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,Q=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,R=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\,\\,\n$$\n\nHence, the combined transformation can be represented by the matrix $RQP:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T & =RQP \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}5 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 5 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$",
